WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.445 --> 00:00:01.800
Three hours from now,

2
00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:04.184
this address will be live on the internet.

3
00:00:04.782 --> 00:00:05.748
Your name.

4
00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:07.236
Your work.

5
00:00:07.805 --> 00:00:10.180
Built by talking, not by coding.

6
00:00:10.645 --> 00:00:12.705
Most portfolios are built once,

7
00:00:12.725 --> 00:00:13.872
on an app builder.

8
00:00:14.459 --> 00:00:16.947
They look fine, and then they never change.

9
00:00:17.504 --> 00:00:19.004
That's a sandcastle.

10
00:00:19.595 --> 00:00:21.280
Today, we build a house:

11
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.129
one you keep adding rooms to.

12
00:00:23.595 --> 00:00:24.742
Here's the plan.

13
00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:25.934
One:

14
00:00:25.954 --> 00:00:28.124
write your idea on one page.

15
00:00:28.715 --> 00:00:29.172
Two:

16
00:00:29.192 --> 00:00:30.650
let Claude interview you,

17
00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:31.874
and research for you.

18
00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:33.104
Three:

19
00:00:33.124 --> 00:00:35.295
turn it into three short documents.

20
00:00:35.885 --> 00:00:36.479
Four:

21
00:00:36.499 --> 00:00:37.934
build it with Claude Code,

22
00:00:37.954 --> 00:00:39.431
one phase at a time.

23
00:00:39.988 --> 00:00:40.718
And five:

24
00:00:40.738 --> 00:00:43.218
push to GitHub, deploy on Cloudflare,

25
00:00:43.238 --> 00:00:44.942
and connect your own domain.

26
00:00:45.408 --> 00:00:46.499
What do you need?

27
00:00:47.074 --> 00:00:48.017
A laptop.

28
00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.187
A free GitHub account.

29
00:00:50.744 --> 00:00:52.247
And a folder of your stuff:

30
00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:55.221
photos, projects, a few lines about you.

31
00:00:55.812 --> 00:00:57.142
Plus curiosity.

32
00:00:57.733 --> 00:00:58.960
Ask questions.

33
00:00:59.562 --> 00:01:00.630
Break things.

34
00:01:01.096 --> 00:01:02.905
In three hours, you walk out with a

35
00:01:02.925 --> 00:01:04.803
live site on your own domain,

36
00:01:04.823 --> 00:01:07.144
a prompt pack, ready templates,

37
00:01:07.164 --> 00:01:08.871
and a way to make it better every

38
00:01:08.891 --> 00:01:09.778
single day.

39
00:01:10.243 --> 00:01:11.618
This isn't theory.

40
00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.366
With the same method,

41
00:01:13.386 --> 00:01:14.923
I built my own site,

42
00:01:14.943 --> 00:01:16.980
a visiting card with five themes,

43
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.048
the Vetal Tekdi birding marathon,

44
00:01:19.068 --> 00:01:22.443
RunFolio, and a data story on pumped storage.

45
00:01:22.909 --> 00:01:24.386
So what's the limit?

46
00:01:24.938 --> 00:01:25.881
Not code.

47
00:01:26.427 --> 00:01:27.495
Not tools.

48
00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.654
Only your imagination.

49
00:01:30.222 --> 00:01:31.495
So let it fly.

50
00:01:32.109 --> 00:01:33.200
Let's begin!
